# Audio Reference Studio

Follow `docs/01_TECHNICAL_MVP_SPEC.md` and `docs/04_TECHNICAL_CHART_REQUIREMENTS.md`. Do not paste them into code or into these rules.

`docs/03_CURSOR_AGENT_FIRST_SESSION.md` is the historical Milestone 0 session. `NEXT_SESSION.md` is an outdated handoff pending human validation of Milestone 1. Neither file accepts a later milestone.

## Milestones

Milestone 0 is `e4f1223`: WAV import, playback, and charts left `not_run`. Milestone 1 is `0f7d7aa`: the analysis worker and charts T01–T10. Preserve that implementation. It is not a validated release. Do not start Milestone 2 (timed lyrics, ZIP export, album comparison, or a narrative client) unless the user asks.

## Architecture

React 19, TypeScript, and Vite on `127.0.0.1:5173`. Python 3.12 and FastAPI on `127.0.0.1:8000`. SQLite plus files under the data root. No cloud, auth, telemetry, payments, or paid API calls.

Frontend owns `frontend/**`. Backend owns `backend/**`. Neither edits the other's tree or `references/legacy-audit/`. Change the API contract before either side depends on it. Regenerate `frontend/src/api/types.ts`; do not hand-edit it.

## Playback

Accepted audio is 16-bit or 24-bit integer PCM WAV. The blob `blobs/{sha256}` stays byte-identical to the upload. A 16-bit master is streamed from that blob, with no derivative. A 24-bit master is streamed from a separate cached file, `derivatives/{sha256}/pcm_s16le-triangular-v1.wav`: FFmpeg writes `pcm_s16le` at the master's sample rate, channel count, and duration, using triangular dither. If that write fails, the import still keeps the master and `playback_status` is `unavailable`.

## Evidence and status

Evidence class describes how a value was obtained: `measured`, `estimated`, `textual`, `interpretive`, `unknown`, or `not_applicable` when a chart does not apply. Tempo, pitch-class, structure, and recurrence stay estimated. State sample rate, channel count, window or hop, and method version with a number. Give the tolerance when a fixture checks it. Do not infer instrumentation, vocal character, mood, or audible defects. Do not claim to have listened. Do not invent sung timestamps.

Status is a different field. Asset `analysis_status` is `not_run`, `queued`, `running`, `completed`, or `failed`. Job status adds `canceled`. Chart status is `not_run`, `ready`, `not_available`, or `failed`. `playback_status` is `ready` or `unavailable`. Do not store an evidence class in a status field, or a status in `evidence_class`.

## Verification

Changes to numerical results, master bytes or hashes, job lifecycle, or HTTP behavior need a pytest, or an extension of an existing one. A UI change that would hide a wrong status or evidence class needs a Vitest when the current test would miss it. A comment, label, or formatting change does not need a new test.

From `backend/`: `uv run ruff check . && uv run pytest -q`

From `frontend/`: `pnpm typecheck && pnpm test && pnpm build`

## Local tools

This repository has no git remote, so Origin cannot see it. Use Graphify only when `graphify-out/` exists. Playwright can set a file input; the Cursor browser cannot.
